* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*    call !acc_tree_count(path, files, bytes, dirs, err)
*
* A per-OS helper of BACKUP.ACCOUNT and RESTORE.ACCOUNT (see !acc_archive).
* dirs counts the directories UNDER path, not path itself.  A reparse point
* anywhere beneath is refused rather than followed.  err is '' or a message
* number then its arguments, value-mark separated.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
subroutine acc_tree_count(path, files, bytes, dirs, err)
$catalog !acc_tree_count

   files = '' ; bytes = '' ; dirs = ''
   counts = ''
   call !acc_archive('COUNT', '', path, counts, err)
   if err # '' then return

   files = counts<1,1>
   bytes = counts<1,2>
   dirs  = counts<1,3>
   return
end
